Date: Sun, 24 Aug 2026 05:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] dosboot: say which partitions the boot scan considers

ISSUE-0051. A whole-disk RDB card with two partitions mounts one of them: DH0,
DOSType FAT\2, appears and boots. DH1, DOSType SFS\0, in the same RDB with the
handler embedded in FSHD/LSEG, produces no device node at all -- "Unknown
device DH1:".

The obvious rejection does not explain it. AddPartitionVolume skips a partition
only when its DosEnvec is too short or its DOSType is zero, and DH1's is
0x53465300. So something else drops it, and this file already reports every
step it takes; the trace was only switched off.

Diagnostic, and loud. Carried only while that is open.
---
--- a/rom/dosboot/bootscan.c
+++ b/rom/dosboot/bootscan.c
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
     Desc: Discover all mountable partitions
 */
 
+#define DEBUG 1
+
 #include <string.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
